+         * logical_h - measured. The estimate it replaces was correct on this dev box (32) and
+         * 2 logical px too large on a build tester's machine (30) -- and that 2px made every
+         * maximized window there permanently unpaintable, because rc_work IS the maximized
+         * window size and a window shorter than the configure never satisfies
+         * wayland_surface_config_is_compatible(). See the write-up in
+         * neutron/dist/HANDOFF-18-root-cause-our-hardcoded-32.md.
+         *
+         * Guarded, because `measured` is process-global while this runs per output: only trust
+         * it for an output whose logical height it could plausibly belong to. A multi-monitor
+         * setup where the maximized window is on the OTHER output falls back to the estimate,
+         * which is exactly the behaviour we have today. */
+        if (measured > 0 && logical_h > 0 && measured <= logical_h &&
+            (logical_h - measured) < logical_h / 4)
+        {
+            logical_inset = logical_h - measured;
+        }
